    description: "`hypergumbo explain <instruction file>` prints a coding-agent instruction file's whole text (default --with-source), while the sketch now lists such files and never quotes them (WI-lufut (b), PR 4).\n\nREPRO (PR 4 branch jgstern-agent/feat/pr4-entry-order-agent-files, commit dd161cf12): a fixture with AGENTS.md holding a sentinel line; `hypergumbo explain AGENTS.md <fixture> --first` prints the sentinel, in both the base and the fixed arm (the fixed arm prints QUOTED_TEXT_NOTICE first, WI-lufut (e)). Owner ruling (b) named the sketch only, so explain was left as it is.\n\nQUESTION: explain is asked for a named target, so printing it may be intended; decide whether explain holds back an instruction file's content the way the sketch does (agent_instructions.py already recognises them). Evidence: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/fast_smart_test_build_11172026/pr4/lufut/RESULTS.md."  # 22a7
